WEBVTT

00:16.070 --> 00:18.600
We're finally arriving in
the Kingdom of Salmutaria.

00:18.600 --> 00:21.480
I wonder what'll be waiting for us here.

00:35.060 --> 00:37.240
What do you make of this situation?

00:37.240 --> 00:40.840
They sure don't look like the guys
Prince Mastoma would've sent for us.

00:40.840 --> 00:42.510
They look like bandits,

00:42.810 --> 00:45.500
but being here the moment
we arrive in Salmutaria?

00:45.500 --> 00:46.890
The timing's too perfect.

00:47.290 --> 00:51.390
I agree. Someone may have set this up.

00:52.970 --> 00:55.890
The ship's far enough
away to be out of danger.

00:56.640 --> 00:57.650
Now...

00:58.070 --> 01:01.630
Shall we catch these guys and
make them cough up who sent them?

01:01.630 --> 01:02.980
I'd say so.

01:04.270 --> 01:06.750
Enough talk. Slaughter them all.

01:18.170 --> 01:25.130
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:40.500 --> 02:41.140
(Episode 19 The Dungeon Count of Welmelia)

02:41.140 --> 02:44.880
(Episode 19 The Dungeon Count of Welmelia)
A bridge on our path here had been destroyed.

02:45.180 --> 02:46.550
(Episode 19 The Dungeon Count of Welmelia)
It made us arrive late.

02:46.550 --> 02:47.010
It made us arrive late.

02:47.430 --> 02:50.340
There's no need for that, Warlock.

02:51.030 --> 02:54.010
I want to speak with you as an equal.

02:54.010 --> 02:56.310
No, Your Highness, I couldn't...

02:56.310 --> 02:57.020
It's fine.

02:57.620 --> 03:01.340
In fact, I can't thank you enough.

03:01.340 --> 03:02.290
Your Highness...

03:03.150 --> 03:08.030
Yuke Feldio, hero and
Dungeon Count of Welmelia,

03:08.350 --> 03:11.090
thank you for agreeing to my request.

03:11.090 --> 03:13.910
I warmly welcome you to Salmutaria.

03:14.400 --> 03:16.970
I'm only returning the favor
you did for us in Duna.

03:16.970 --> 03:19.040
I mean... I...

03:19.330 --> 03:21.190
You're repaying more than you owe.

03:21.190 --> 03:24.500
Regardless, I'm glad you're all safe.

03:24.500 --> 03:25.040
Yes.

03:25.580 --> 03:26.960
So who were they?

03:26.960 --> 03:30.050
It seems my older brother sent them.

03:30.410 --> 03:32.270
Your older brother?

03:32.270 --> 03:35.860
I have several siblings competing
with me for the throne.

03:35.860 --> 03:38.010
I'm especially incompatible with Rafuma,

03:38.010 --> 03:40.060
who's a year older than me.

03:40.060 --> 03:40.810
I see...

03:41.200 --> 03:43.840
He's even tried to kill me before.

03:43.840 --> 03:46.310
I beat him at his own
game every time, though.

03:46.690 --> 03:48.840
Take them back and interrogate them.

03:48.840 --> 03:50.000
And be courteous.

03:50.000 --> 03:50.820
Yes, Your Highness!

03:50.820 --> 03:53.180
Still, yes...

03:53.180 --> 03:56.700
You and your party will need
to be careful, as well.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.500
Regarding this Prince Rafuma...

03:59.500 --> 04:03.460
Would you mind if I told Benwood
and the rest of Clover about him?

04:04.360 --> 04:07.250
My relationship with him
is common knowledge.

04:07.250 --> 04:08.290
Share it as you please.

04:08.290 --> 04:09.670
Thank you.

04:11.410 --> 04:12.800
Now, Yuke...

04:13.190 --> 04:14.050
Yes?

04:14.360 --> 04:16.010
You're being too polite!

04:16.010 --> 04:17.300
Be more casual!

04:18.420 --> 04:22.920
Lord Feldio, my husband
wishes to be your friend.

04:22.920 --> 04:23.560
Huh?

04:24.060 --> 04:24.890
Mejarna!

04:24.890 --> 04:28.690
Darling, if you want Lord Feldio
to be more casual,

04:28.690 --> 04:32.420
you must speak more casually to him.

04:32.920 --> 04:35.650
It must be you who speaks on his level.

04:35.650 --> 04:36.400
Right...

04:36.400 --> 04:37.450
Oh, no, I—

04:38.440 --> 04:40.450
Call me Mastoma, Yuke!

04:43.240 --> 04:44.480
What should I do?

04:44.480 --> 04:45.920
I think it's okay.

04:45.920 --> 04:48.110
Rhaenys! You're doing well?

04:48.110 --> 04:50.550
I'm just Rain, Your Highness.

04:50.920 --> 04:52.930
Ah, that's right.

04:52.930 --> 04:54.810
Thank you for doing this for me.

04:54.810 --> 04:57.650
Oh, no. I haven't done anything.

04:57.650 --> 04:59.680
It was Yuke's decision.

05:00.560 --> 05:02.810
A fine wife, elevating her husband!

05:04.520 --> 05:06.940
It's good to see you again, Lady Mejarna.

05:07.250 --> 05:10.150
Yes. I'm glad to see you are well, Rain.

05:10.660 --> 05:11.740
Lord Feldio.

05:11.740 --> 05:12.600
Y-Yes?

05:12.600 --> 05:15.820
Please do become my husband's friend.

05:16.230 --> 05:22.500
It's very unusual to see him
behaving as adorably as he is now.

05:24.370 --> 05:28.960
If you wouldn't mind... I'd love
to be friends, uh... Mastoma.

05:29.830 --> 05:32.080
No! More casual!

05:32.080 --> 05:34.460
You're making me look weak and foolish!

05:36.850 --> 05:38.600
Okay, Mastoma.

05:38.600 --> 05:40.720
I'm honestly just a peasant
from the countryside,

05:41.000 --> 05:43.470
so I might end up being
rude to you sometimes.

05:43.470 --> 05:44.550
Is that okay?

05:44.550 --> 05:47.230
Yes! I would be most pleased!

05:47.540 --> 05:49.480
Well, okay, then...

05:52.790 --> 05:55.230
Now, let us head for Ra-jo.

05:55.500 --> 05:56.610
Ra-jo?

05:56.970 --> 05:59.650
That's the town I had built for you.

05:59.650 --> 06:02.680
In Salmutarian, it means "hope."

06:02.680 --> 06:04.370
Precisely, Rhaenys...

06:04.690 --> 06:06.180
I mean, Rain.

06:06.180 --> 06:10.340
It is the place that represents new
hope for this kingdom, after all.

06:13.130 --> 06:15.630
(2 Days Later)

06:16.130 --> 06:20.130
(Mountain Town Under the Second Prince's
Supervision, Ra-jo)

06:26.740 --> 06:28.780
Wow, it's so pretty!

06:28.780 --> 06:30.440
It's shining!

06:30.440 --> 06:33.560
It really lives up to
the "hope" of its name!

06:34.630 --> 06:36.810
Welcome to Ra-jo!

06:38.850 --> 06:43.570
I'm surprised they built such a
nice town in mountains like these.

06:43.850 --> 06:45.560
And in such a short time...

06:45.560 --> 06:47.580
You're amazing, Prince!

06:47.870 --> 06:51.400
Oh, you think so?
Feel free to praise me more!

06:51.400 --> 06:54.910
Darling, you mustn't get too carried away.

06:54.910 --> 06:56.840
I know, I know.

06:58.130 --> 07:01.090
This is where the revolution will begin.

07:07.720 --> 07:10.600
So this is Ra-jo's Adventurer's Guild, eh?

07:10.920 --> 07:13.180
It looks quite impressive.

07:13.180 --> 07:15.610
If there's anything you need,
I'll have it arranged.

07:15.870 --> 07:18.070
No need to be modest, Lord Benwood.

07:18.070 --> 07:22.530
Oh? In that case, why don't I have you
bring some of Salmutaria's finest liquor?

07:22.530 --> 07:24.120
C-Come on, Benwood!

07:25.630 --> 07:27.120
Of course! I shall arrange it!

07:27.400 --> 07:29.440
Hey, you do get it!

07:29.440 --> 07:32.170
I think you and I are
gonna get along just fine!

07:36.000 --> 07:37.630
Yuke, here it is.

07:37.630 --> 07:40.210
Wow, this is a pretty impressive mansion.

07:40.210 --> 07:40.940
And?

07:42.610 --> 07:45.600
You can be quite dense at times.

07:46.010 --> 07:50.670
I'm telling you that this is the
Welmelian adventuring ambassador,

07:50.670 --> 07:52.460
Dungeon Count Feldio's, personal mansion.

07:52.460 --> 07:54.350
We're going to live here?!

07:55.210 --> 07:56.840
Yuke, look.

07:58.400 --> 08:00.150
(Welmelian Adventuring Ambassador,)
"Welmelian Adventuring Ambassador,
Dungeon Count Yuke Feldio"?!

08:00.150 --> 08:02.360
(Dungeon Count Yuke Feldio)
"Welmelian Adventuring Ambassador,
Dungeon Count Yuke Feldio"?!

08:02.630 --> 08:03.480
Whoa, now...

08:03.480 --> 08:05.290
It's very big...

08:05.290 --> 08:09.870
Isn't it? I'm quite proud of
its readiness to host guests!

08:10.120 --> 08:12.990
Wait, this is much too big for me!

08:12.990 --> 08:15.940
Well, a bit of decadence
is needed in this case.

08:16.680 --> 08:20.010
You're a Welmelian dungeon
count with five wives.

08:21.930 --> 08:25.000
One, two, three, four, five...

08:27.270 --> 08:29.600
An adventurer recognized as a hero,

08:29.600 --> 08:32.510
and friend to Mastoma,
who is vying for the throne.

08:32.510 --> 08:35.670
If I were to give someone like that
a cheap place to stay,

08:35.670 --> 08:39.400
some fools out there would start
questioning things needlessly.

08:39.880 --> 08:45.150
I get it. You did this to show
people that you're serious.

08:45.480 --> 08:48.250
In that case, we'll use it with gratitude.

08:48.250 --> 08:51.410
Good! Then I'll have your
things brought in at once.

08:58.980 --> 09:00.660
Thank you.

09:03.500 --> 09:05.420
I feel more relaxed now.

09:05.720 --> 09:06.580
Same here.

09:08.250 --> 09:11.770
I guess we're just waiting for construction
on the guild facility to wrap up.

09:11.770 --> 09:14.930
But still, we can't just
sit around daydreaming.

09:15.200 --> 09:17.550
Let's go visit the market tomorrow.

09:17.550 --> 09:20.010
We need to get an idea
of what they sell here.

09:20.010 --> 09:22.700
Mastoma said he'll get us
everything we need

09:22.700 --> 09:24.940
if we just give him a list.

09:24.940 --> 09:27.060
Let's figure out what we'll need.

09:27.060 --> 09:27.570
Right.

09:28.150 --> 09:30.440
There are lots of other
things we need to do too.

09:30.440 --> 09:34.580
Figure out the lay of the land,
see what monsters live here...

09:34.860 --> 09:39.960
And check the route to the dungeon
that the prince says he knows, right?

09:40.270 --> 09:41.050
Yep.

09:42.970 --> 09:44.960
It's so quiet. Where are the others?

09:45.640 --> 09:48.760
They must have been exhausted.
They're already asleep.

09:49.070 --> 09:52.230
Well, those beds are
impossibly comfortable.

09:52.230 --> 09:58.140
I bet Mastoma could become an
accomplished king just by exporting those.

09:59.070 --> 10:00.370
Definitely!

10:01.990 --> 10:05.480
The stars look the same
as they do in Welmelia.

10:05.480 --> 10:07.470
Do they look different where you're from?

10:07.470 --> 10:13.160
Yes, the stars visible from my homeland,
Vilmullen, look a bit different.

10:14.230 --> 10:17.010
It's been, what, three years
since you left the island?

10:17.010 --> 10:18.370
Do you ever miss it?

10:18.690 --> 10:20.440
Not at all.

10:20.440 --> 10:22.710
I have all of you now.

10:22.710 --> 10:25.500
But I feel a little nostalgic at times.

10:25.810 --> 10:28.320
I'd like to go back someday.

10:28.320 --> 10:30.600
I see. I'd like to visit, too.

10:30.600 --> 10:33.850
Oh, humans aren't very
welcome there, though.

10:33.850 --> 10:36.140
Oh... I guess they wouldn't be, huh?

10:36.670 --> 10:39.930
But I'd love to have you there!

10:39.930 --> 10:41.020
Thanks.

10:41.310 --> 10:45.800
But of course, completing this
king's order comes first.

10:45.800 --> 10:46.530
Yeah.

10:46.830 --> 10:48.600
I'm counting on you, Silk.

10:48.600 --> 10:49.990
Of course, Master.

10:51.030 --> 10:54.030
(2 Weeks Later)

10:54.030 --> 10:57.290
(Ra-jo Adventurer's Guild)

10:57.620 --> 11:01.690
From Ra-jo, you need to pass through
Death Valley to reach the dungeon.

11:01.690 --> 11:03.290
It's believed to be around here.

11:03.980 --> 11:08.310
According to legend, it is the grave of
my distant ancestors, a royal mausoleum.

11:08.310 --> 11:09.770
Thanks, Mastoma.

11:09.770 --> 11:13.300
Then Clover will explore Death Valley

11:13.300 --> 11:15.540
while we clear a path to the mausoleum.

11:15.540 --> 11:16.060
Good.

11:16.360 --> 11:22.340
I'll continue to inspect the large
streaming artifacts set up around Ra-jo.

11:22.340 --> 11:24.700
It seems they're taking a while
to adjust to the ley lines

11:24.700 --> 11:26.510
and haven't started working yet.

11:26.510 --> 11:27.770
I'll be counting on you.

11:27.770 --> 11:29.440
What about you, Benwood?

11:29.750 --> 11:33.660
I'm swamped with preparations for
the background checks of

11:33.660 --> 11:35.950
Salmutarians who applied
to be adventurers-in-training.

11:36.460 --> 11:39.210
Sorry to ask, Yuke, but could
you let me borrow Jamie?

11:39.210 --> 11:40.670
I'm shorthanded.

11:40.670 --> 11:41.460
Jamie?

11:41.790 --> 11:45.000
Jamie worked at the guild
for over six months,

11:45.000 --> 11:46.090
so she's used to it. Right?

11:46.420 --> 11:49.160
I'm fine with that if Jamie doesn't mind,

11:49.160 --> 11:50.340
but why ask me?

11:50.690 --> 11:53.330
She's a member of Clover, isn't she?

11:53.330 --> 11:56.220
And you're Clover's leader.
Of course I'd ask for your permission.

11:56.700 --> 11:59.020
That makes sense. Do you mind, Jamie?

11:59.020 --> 12:00.470
Not a problem.

12:00.470 --> 12:04.230
I'll be Mamar's substitute.
No choice, really.

12:04.610 --> 12:05.770
I appreciate it.

12:06.840 --> 12:08.660
What about me?

12:08.660 --> 12:11.100
Would you mind staying here for me?

12:11.100 --> 12:12.030
Aw...

12:12.360 --> 12:13.890
We're just scoping things out first.

12:13.890 --> 12:16.680
I'm sure we'll be needing you later.

12:16.680 --> 12:18.740
Come adventuring with us then, okay?

12:19.030 --> 12:20.350
You promise?

12:20.350 --> 12:21.770
I promise.

12:21.770 --> 12:25.410
So for now, I'd like you
to help Benwood and Jamie.

12:25.410 --> 12:26.630
Would you, Rune?

12:26.910 --> 12:30.880
Sure, I'll help!
You guys be careful, okay?

12:31.210 --> 12:33.780
Right. Let's have fun, but be careful!

12:39.010 --> 12:42.520
(Death Valley)

12:42.520 --> 12:45.270
I can see why they call it Death Valley.

12:46.300 --> 12:49.400
Yuke, I'll hold on to the magic gems.

12:49.760 --> 12:50.510
Thanks.

12:50.940 --> 12:52.860
It's so vast and complex.

12:52.860 --> 12:55.960
This valley might as well
be a dungeon itself.

12:55.960 --> 12:57.780
It does have a lot of monsters.

12:57.780 --> 13:00.030
And there's no safety area.

13:00.360 --> 13:01.870
It's extremely dangerous.

13:01.870 --> 13:03.830
No wonder they call it Death Valley.

13:03.830 --> 13:04.770
Master!

13:05.520 --> 13:07.190
Something isn't right.

13:07.190 --> 13:08.730
Did you find something?

13:08.730 --> 13:11.890
The spirit energy in this area
is disturbed.

13:11.890 --> 13:14.360
I wouldn't call it chaotic,

13:14.360 --> 13:17.180
but there's a spirit that's
behaving strangely.

13:17.490 --> 13:21.560
If the spirits, the beings that make
up this world, are disturbed...

13:22.510 --> 13:25.670
Does that mean Death Valley is unstable?

13:28.630 --> 13:30.420
Let's be very careful.

13:30.920 --> 13:33.500
It's possible there's an
Overflow going on.

13:33.500 --> 13:37.570
I hope that's all it is,
but I have a bad feeling...

13:38.000 --> 13:39.820
Are you okay, Yuke?

13:40.370 --> 13:42.700
Actually, something feels off.

13:43.020 --> 13:47.210
What if the seal on the dungeon—the
royal mausoleum—really is gone?

13:47.550 --> 13:49.810
We'll let Mastoma know first.

13:49.810 --> 13:53.590
We don't know if it's an
Overflow, a Stampede, or...

13:53.590 --> 13:55.340
Another culling?

13:56.420 --> 13:59.590
I really don't want that
guess to be on the mark.

13:59.930 --> 14:02.680
I think we should take
our time investigating.

14:02.680 --> 14:04.470
That means camping out. Is that okay?

14:04.470 --> 14:08.130
Not a problem. Plan B it is, then.

14:08.130 --> 14:10.440
It's been a while since we camped out!

14:10.440 --> 14:13.940
Oh, but we can't do an adventure
cooking stream yet, can we?

14:14.290 --> 14:17.420
We might be able to get
a connection from Ra-jo.

14:17.420 --> 14:21.010
We'll have to place our hopes in the
artifacts Viscount Bodeman set up.

14:21.010 --> 14:21.700
Yep!

14:21.700 --> 14:23.700
Make sure you're recording, okay?

14:23.700 --> 14:25.160
Understood!

14:25.160 --> 14:26.450
Leave it to us!

14:37.150 --> 14:38.280
What do you think?

14:38.280 --> 14:39.840
Something still feels off.

14:40.180 --> 14:43.400
It's coming from the direction he
said the royal mausoleum was in.

14:43.400 --> 14:45.350
Yeah. I feel it, too.

14:45.650 --> 14:46.520
Master.

14:46.520 --> 14:47.220
What's up?

14:47.520 --> 14:50.980
Let's go over our plans for tomorrow
before we call it a night.

14:51.280 --> 14:52.300
Good idea.

14:55.320 --> 14:58.420
First, we'll confirm the exact
location of the royal mausoleum.

14:58.420 --> 15:01.300
If possible, we'll check the inside.

15:01.300 --> 15:05.490
Even if we can't go that far, I'd like
to get a feel for the surroundings.

15:05.790 --> 15:09.300
And see whether an Overflow
is really happening or not.

15:09.300 --> 15:10.410
Right.

15:10.710 --> 15:13.000
What should we do about getting back?

15:13.000 --> 15:15.060
If the investigation takes a long time,

15:15.060 --> 15:17.660
we'll rest here again before
returning to our lodging.

15:17.660 --> 15:19.800
I don't want us to push too
hard in an unfamiliar area.

15:22.610 --> 15:24.050
Yuke, this is...

15:24.360 --> 15:25.420
I know.

15:26.850 --> 15:30.640
This is weird! I've never felt
anything like this before!

15:30.640 --> 15:31.810
Calm down, Nene.

15:32.150 --> 15:33.480
We're depending on you.

15:33.480 --> 15:35.400
Can you check our surroundings?

15:35.400 --> 15:36.790
I'm on it!

15:36.790 --> 15:38.410
Don't push yourself too hard.

15:38.410 --> 15:39.570
Just find out what's going on.

15:39.880 --> 15:40.570
Got it!

15:42.330 --> 15:43.830
This strange presence...

15:43.830 --> 15:46.080
Master, I'm scared.

15:46.400 --> 15:47.960
It's okay, Silk.

15:47.960 --> 15:50.500
Whatever happens, I'll take care of it.

15:50.500 --> 15:54.080
This feeling must be part of the presence
that's coming from the royal mausoleum.

15:54.080 --> 15:56.860
It should still be
pretty far off, though...

15:56.860 --> 15:59.010
How is it reaching this far?

15:59.010 --> 16:00.100
Trouble!

16:00.100 --> 16:00.970
What's going on?

16:00.970 --> 16:03.880
There's an army of monsters to the east!

16:03.880 --> 16:05.590
Around twenty of them!

16:05.900 --> 16:06.850
What type?

16:07.630 --> 16:08.640
It's a mix.

16:09.130 --> 16:10.720
That's bad!

16:10.720 --> 16:11.640
Why?

16:11.900 --> 16:18.900
Usually, the monsters that escape a dungeon
in an Overflow are all the same type.

16:19.180 --> 16:23.400
You mean something even worse
than an Overflow is happening?

16:24.260 --> 16:25.910
Like a Stampede?

16:26.190 --> 16:27.780
A Stampede?

16:28.060 --> 16:30.670
No, we can't say that for sure yet.

16:30.670 --> 16:31.370
Silk.

16:31.370 --> 16:32.040
Yes?

16:32.310 --> 16:34.840
Do you think we can get back to
Ra-jo before the night's over?

16:34.840 --> 16:38.950
Yes. There are risks, but just
going back should be possible.

16:38.950 --> 16:40.420
Okay, good.

16:41.920 --> 16:43.760
Did you all hear that?

16:43.760 --> 16:47.200
We'll have to push ourselves hard,
but we're going straight back to Ra-jo!

16:47.200 --> 16:49.930
Roger! I'll lead the way!

16:50.240 --> 16:53.240
Silk, ask Biblion to be on
watch for surprise attacks.

16:53.240 --> 16:54.440
Understood.

16:54.760 --> 16:56.930
Rain, use detection magic.

16:56.930 --> 16:58.190
Okay, got it.

16:58.500 --> 17:01.370
We haven't found out what
monsters come out at night yet.

17:01.370 --> 17:03.800
If we run into them,
we'll be fighting blind.

17:03.800 --> 17:04.950
Let's go.

17:05.220 --> 17:06.910
Marina, you're our rear guard.

17:06.910 --> 17:07.950
I'm on it!

17:08.230 --> 17:10.310
I'll restore our health.

17:10.310 --> 17:11.580
Run as fast as you can!

17:11.880 --> 17:13.120
Physical Enchant!

17:13.330 --> 17:14.330
(Enhanced Arm Strength, Enhanced
Leg Strength, Enhanced Stamina)

17:14.840 --> 17:15.830
Let's go!

17:22.280 --> 17:24.720
Two lizards ahead and to the right!

17:25.020 --> 17:26.090
Sleep Mist!

17:26.090 --> 17:29.090
(Sleep Mist)

17:40.190 --> 17:41.070
Master!

17:41.070 --> 17:41.860
What's up?

17:42.220 --> 17:44.260
I realized it when night fell.

17:44.260 --> 17:47.990
This valley is definitely being
influenced by a dungeon transformation!

17:48.480 --> 17:49.490
What does that mean?

17:49.810 --> 17:54.120
Is it the prelude to a Stampede
or the growth of a dungeon?

17:54.450 --> 17:59.880
I don't know, but if we're not careful,
it could affect all of Salmutaria!

18:01.000 --> 18:02.130
Nene, over here.

18:02.360 --> 18:04.630
Rain? That's a cliff!

18:05.160 --> 18:06.990
We had to climb it to get here,

18:06.990 --> 18:08.800
but to get back, we just have to go down.

18:09.330 --> 18:11.770
Sky into earth, and earth into sky...

18:11.770 --> 18:14.680
All things flow into one another,
eliminating boundaries.

18:15.010 --> 18:16.560
Falling Control!

18:16.560 --> 18:18.310
(Falling Control)

18:19.870 --> 18:20.770
Behind us!

18:20.770 --> 18:22.310
Seven monsters, mixed typing!

18:23.700 --> 18:24.320
Jump!

18:24.680 --> 18:26.150
Yah!

18:35.480 --> 18:36.920
Nice work, Rain.

18:36.920 --> 18:38.080
Refresh Mana.

18:39.400 --> 18:40.300
Yeah.

18:40.300 --> 18:43.500
There are still a few other spots
where we can use shortcuts.

18:43.790 --> 18:44.850
Leave them to me.

18:44.850 --> 18:47.260
We're almost there. Let's hurry!

18:52.530 --> 18:53.800
Three to the left!

18:58.520 --> 18:59.890
Critical Weapon!

19:01.970 --> 19:03.340
Okay, let's move!

19:19.110 --> 19:22.540
And that concludes our report.

19:23.860 --> 19:26.300
Well, this has turned into quite a mess.

19:26.600 --> 19:29.330
I've checked over the footage
you recorded.

19:29.330 --> 19:33.100
Given the many types of monsters
you encountered on your way back,

19:33.100 --> 19:36.310
this does indeed look like
the prelude to a Stampede.

19:36.310 --> 19:37.310
I see.

19:37.890 --> 19:40.010
Dignitaries of Welmelia,

19:40.010 --> 19:44.060
how do you handle these
situations in your country?

19:44.360 --> 19:46.330
Well, at this scale,

19:46.330 --> 19:50.130
we'll select multiple adventuring
parties to undertake a mission

19:50.130 --> 19:53.320
to thin out the monsters'
numbers and find out the cause.

19:53.640 --> 19:57.950
We may also consider sending in
the army or the knights.

19:58.300 --> 20:01.330
But Salmutaria has neither of those.

20:02.300 --> 20:06.460
Sir Benwood, would it be possible
to send adventurers from abroad?

20:06.780 --> 20:09.600
With your permission
and enough money, yes.

20:09.600 --> 20:13.020
But adventurers are still human, you know.

20:13.020 --> 20:17.470
Transporting a lot of them over national
borders can become a bit problematic.

20:17.810 --> 20:21.250
All right. I will ask my
father for permission.

20:21.250 --> 20:22.430
You will?

20:22.750 --> 20:26.300
I thought only you knew
about the royal mausoleum.

20:26.300 --> 20:28.450
If you disclose that information,

20:28.450 --> 20:31.060
won't the siblings competing with
you for the throne take issue?

20:31.060 --> 20:31.690
Let them.

20:32.070 --> 20:35.190
I'm concerned not with my own standing,

20:35.190 --> 20:38.040
but with protecting my
country and its people.

20:38.040 --> 20:41.210
Besides, I can tell from
the look on your face

20:41.210 --> 20:43.210
that this is a grave situation.

20:45.050 --> 20:48.780
I formally request the deployment
of adventurers from Welmelia.

20:48.780 --> 20:50.580
I will assume all responsibility.

20:52.770 --> 20:55.220
I apologize, but please help me.

20:55.550 --> 20:56.550
Mastoma...

20:56.550 --> 20:57.750
H-Hey, now...

20:57.750 --> 20:58.720
You mustn't...

20:59.080 --> 21:02.550
As I am not yet king,
there is little I can do.

21:02.550 --> 21:05.810
But if it means I can save
my country and its people,

21:05.810 --> 21:08.580
I will bow my head
as many times as it takes.

21:08.580 --> 21:09.730
Please!

21:12.760 --> 21:13.990
All right.

21:16.900 --> 21:20.270
Mastoma, we'll do everything we can.

21:22.290 --> 21:23.450
You have my word.

22:56.000 --> 22:57.380
(The World Turns Inside-Out)

22:57.380 --> 22:59.770
(The World Turns Inside-Out)
Next time, "The World Turns Inside-Out."

22:59.770 --> 23:01.010
(The World Turns Inside-Out)
